  "query_preview": "../Friday through Monday/...\nNo major changes to be seen in the extended forecast with a ridge\nof high pressure building in over the gulf come Friday. This will\nfinally dislodge the weak troughing over the panhandle and usher \nin more consistent dry conditions this weekend and overall benign \nweather. As mentioned in previous discussions, a tightening \ngradient early Friday favoring north south oriented channels is \nexpected to bring about some stout northerly winds. However these \nshould quickly diminish through the afternoon hours Friday with \nwinds across the inner channels and coastal waters largely falling\nto 10 kt or less. With the drier conditions, localized sea \nbreezes are expected through the weekend but should not be \nparticularly impactful. \n\nThe main question in the long term remains whether a low develops\nin the northern gulf to take a swipe at the northern panhandle \nearly next week. Models are still not sold on the idea, though \nthere is a slight trend for a majority of the associated \nprecipitation to remain over the interior. Overall though the main\ntakeaway is still for another round of more summer-like weather \nthis weekend with fairly dry conditions and daytime highs to \nrebound to the mid 60s to around 70 for most of the panhandle.",
